@@ -9,6 +9,19 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local resources
+
+Open **Local network** in the header, choose a local network device or this
+computer (loopback), enter its HTTP(S) resource URL, and select **Connect**.
+Requests run in the user's browser, so localhost refers to the user's computer.
+The page displays the HTTP status and up to 64 KB of response text.
+
+Deploy the application over HTTPS. Access is subject to browser permission and
+the resource server's CORS configuration (allow the application's origin).
+Browsers without Local Network Access support still attempt the request on
+Connect, but may require HTTPS on the resource as well. If access is blocked,
+update the site's Local network or Loopback network permission and retry.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
